41️⃣ Compare and contrast for, while, and do-while loops with syntax and example.

Feature	for Loop	while Loop	do-while Loop

Condition check	Before execution	Before execution	After execution
Execution guarantee	May not execute	May not execute	Executes at least once
Best used when	Number of iterations known	Condition-based looping	At least one execution needed


Syntax & Examples:

✔ for loop

for(int i=1; i<=5; i++){
    printf("%d", i);
}

✔ while loop

int i = 1;
while(i <= 5){
    printf("%d", i);
    i++;
}

✔ do-while loop

int i = 1;
do{
    printf("%d", i);
    i++;
} while(i <= 5);


